      "text": "(a) Unfair methods of competition in commerce and unfair or deceptive acts or practices in commerce are hereby declared unlawful.",
      "text_sha256": "5ce4cdc5cf6971b1ad3dbc83315353961d9d7819d6050ef21f1acfae1c8a5493",
      "publisher_sha256": "4a8f7bb70c77d8bc001fa479e705523f42399d42448c4260eed92bdce781e80c",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-17T21:03:58.568863+00:00",
      "currentness": "unresolved",
      "language": "en"
    },
    "9a49c93f2d9050d1671ee167a86468": {
      "source_id": "US-VT:contract_formation:717f8d4e7c23",
      "authority_type": "statute",
      "citation": "9A V.S.A. § 2-204",
      "text": "A contract for sale of goods may be made in any manner sufficient to show agreement, including conduct by both parties which recognizes the existence of such a contract.",
      "text_sha256": "9c77be9f087223530e0d86a71047d66373e3a4889718dffe0aff6b1ded1679b9",
